# Redirects for Cloudflare Pages. Pages serves /guides from guides.html on its
# own and redirects the .html spelling, so these three lines are belt and
# braces: they keep the behaviour stated in the repo rather than inherited from
# a host default, and they are what gets checked after a host change.
#
# Unlike the Caddy block, this cannot be a regex. A new page needs a new line
# here, or it keeps whatever Pages does by default.

/index.html         /             301
/guides.html        /guides       301
/whitepaper.html    /whitepaper   301

# www to apex is deliberately NOT here. Caddy did it with a host matcher, but
# this file matches on path only: a source written as a full URL is accepted by
# wrangler without complaint and then never fires, which is exactly how it was
# found. On Pages that redirect is a zone-level Redirect Rule instead, so it
# lives in the Cloudflare dashboard rather than in this repo. See deploy/README.
